Two monitors for two recurring blind spots, both from the 2026-09-03
incidents:

1. scripts/gate_cascade_check.py (REQ-CONDUCTOR-CASCADE-1): joins the
   active roadmap's gates against the artifacts on disk and reports any
   gate whose upstream EXISTS and already fails — the exp6942 shape that
   took 10 of 12 tasks in milestone 608. Absent upstream is deliberately
   silent (the hand-tested discrimination: fires on 608, silent on all
   seven of 609's gates). Reuses conductor_gates primitives so it cannot
   drift from activation-time evaluation. Wired into the outer-loop
   dashboard; first live run found exp6977.certified_pwa_energy_ready_
   score=0 with exp6982 gating on it (already blocked by detection time,
   annotated as such).

2. scripts/conductor_heartbeat_sampler.py (REQ-CONDUCTOR-WCHAN-1): the
   non-privileged replacement for the unexecutable py-spy remedy. One
   JSONL record per minute — wchan, State line, pgrep -P child count —
   via the carnot-heartbeat-sampler systemd user timer (enabled;
   production sample verified 16:38:04Z). Samples live outside the repo
   in ~/.carnot/heartbeat_samples/ so they never churn git status.

Mutation-proven: cascade firing rule disabled -> 2 RED, naive
absent-counts-as-finding rule -> 1 RED, both restored byte-identically
-> 6 GREEN; sampler wchan read dropped -> 2 RED, restored -> 4 GREEN.

